# Frontend UI work

Before changing anything visual in `frontend/`, read the vendored design skill:

- `.cursor/skills/taste-skill/PROJECT-NOTES.md` first. It has the design read,
  the dial values, the list of upstream rules this project overrides and why,
  and the seven house rules. It is short.
- `.cursor/skills/taste-skill/skills/redesign-skill/SKILL.md` when changing
  existing screens. It is the audit checklist this frontend was brought up to.
- `.cursor/skills/taste-skill/skills/taste-skill/SKILL.md` for the full
  reference. Note its section 13: it scopes itself out of dashboards and data
  tables, which is most of this app. `PROJECT-NOTES.md` records which sections
  apply here and which do not.
- `.cursor/skills/taste-skill/UPSTREAM.md` for provenance and for the procedure
  to refresh the vendored copy from upstream.

## Non-negotiables

1. Use the semantic tokens in `frontend/src/index.css` (`surface`,
   `surface-raised`, `surface-sunken`, `line`, `ink`, `ink-muted`, `ink-subtle`,
   `accent`). Raw palette literals such as `bg-gray-800` are drift. Tailwind's
   `emerald`, `amber`, and `red` are allowed only for real semantic state.
2. Build from `frontend/src/components/ui/` before writing new markup. Adding
   another bespoke button or modal is how the previous inconsistency happened.
3. Blue is the only accent. One radius rule: pills for status badges,
   `rounded-md` for controls, `rounded-lg` for surfaces.
4. Every async view ships four states: skeleton shaped like the real content,
   empty state with a next action, error state with a retry, success.
5. Keyboard and screen readers are part of done. Real `<button>` and `<a>`
   elements, a visible `focus-visible` ring, labelled form controls, overlays
   that trap focus and close on Escape and restore focus on close.
6. No em-dash characters anywhere, in UI strings or in code. Use a hyphen, a
   comma, or two sentences.
7. Motion stays at CSS transitions on `transform`, `opacity`, `color`, and
   `background-color`, gated by the `prefers-reduced-motion` block already in
   `index.css`. Do not add an animation library.
8. Reuse before installing. Check `frontend/package.json` first, and prefer an
   existing dependency or a few lines of local code over a new package.

## Keeping the skill current

Do not edit anything under `.cursor/skills/taste-skill/skills/` or its
`LICENSE`. Those are a verbatim upstream copy, pinned to a commit, so that
refreshing is a clean replace. Project opinions go in `PROJECT-NOTES.md`.
`UPSTREAM.md` has the update commands and the checks to run afterwards.

## Validation

From `frontend/`: `npm run lint`, `npm run build` (runs `tsc -b` first), and
`npm run test`. All three must pass. Backend contracts are fixed: do not change
API request or response shapes, route paths, or query keys to suit the UI.
